From 657b38884f39d3669496b3a589b95a0f7f48caf3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: pypto-x-agent <pypto-x-agent@local>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 00:49:40 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 115/144] fix(cuda): make the cuEvent self-proof prove the
 timer rate, not raw equality

The WSL2 RTX 5080 host has a platform cuEvent rate offset: a 5.000 s host
sleep inside a single event pair measures 4.70-4.77 s on the device clock,
and a 19 s GPU batch measures 17.60 s by events against 18.70 s on an
independent third clock.  A raw event-vs-wall threshold therefore cannot
pass on this platform, and the earlier gate was unstable.

Redesign the smoke self-proof around in-run calibration:
- rate stability: two known host-sleep gaps inside one event pair give
  event_timer_rate = host_wall / event_span (spread gate <= 3%);
- linearity: per-launch event time from an R/2 and an R batch must agree
  within 3%;
- corrected wall agreement: batch_event * event_timer_rate vs host wall
  within 5%.

Raw values remain in kernel_seconds (protocol field) with the corrected
best estimate in kernel_seconds_corrected; raw disagreement is reported
explicitly (raw_wall_agreement=false, platform_flags=
[wsl2_cuevent_rate_offset]).  Also make timing_error truthful when the
driver lacks the event API (an explicit timing=False opt-out stays None),
report peak_rss_mib/peak_device_memory_mib and use the protocol's
nearest-rank p95 (p95_linear kept for comparison).
