+host the CUDA event clock itself runs ~6% slow relative to the host wall
+clock (measured in-run; see ``timer_calibration``), independent of kernel
+size.  A raw event-vs-wall threshold therefore cannot pass on this platform.
+Instead the gate proves the right quantity:
+
+1. rate stability: two known host ``time.sleep`` gaps inside a single event
